# =====================================================================
# Saleor Discounts domain — P3 wave, packet A3: the promotion/voucher
# read roots (the canonical plan §5-P3: "discounts, gift cards ... map
# to the existing pricing owner"). PROPOSAL to A0 (the one SDL
# steward): the Query fields below append to the shared root type
# Query; every other declaration in this fragment is a PURE ADDITION —
# no existing shared type is redeclared (PageInfo, OrderDirection,
# PermissionEnum, the User/Group families, the ProductType family and
# the StoreProduct*/Service*/Discovery*/Neighborhood* legacy roots
# keep their existing declarations).
# Root names, argument names/types/nullability and the connection
# envelope are the pinned Saleor 3.23.43 wire contract
# (saleor/graphql/schema.graphql, blob b8fa0dd8 — the measured roots
# voucher/vouchers at schema lines 1198/1218 and promotion/promotions
# at 1253/1270, the Voucher type at line 11315, DiscountValueTypeEnum
# at 11643, VoucherCountableConnection/Edge at 17268/17277,
# VoucherFilterInput at 17285, VoucherSortingInput at 17301,
# VoucherSortField at 17312, the Promotion type at 17353,
# PromotionTypeEnum at 17433, PromotionCountableConnection/Edge at
# 17707/17716, PromotionWhereInput at 17724, PromotionSortingInput at
# 17754, PromotionSortField at 17762); the platform's pricing owner
# remains the single source of truth behind them. The GLOBAL IDs on
# this surface are the typed Relay-style codec's
# (SaleorGlobalIdCodec): opaque base64("Promotion:<uuid>") /
# base64("Voucher:<uuid>") values — never raw UUIDs.
#
# PERMISSIONS (verified against the pinned schema, not the ledger):
# all four roots carry Saleor's own annotation "Requires one of the
# following permissions: MANAGE_DISCOUNTS" (schema lines 1194/1214/
# 1249/1267). The campaign ledger's row for `promotions` says
# MANAGE_PRODUCTS — a transcription error reported to A0 in the
# completion report; either staff requirement maps to the platform's
# ADMIN capability at the pricing use-case boundary (the RBAC mapping
# registry row), never a UI route guard.
#
# The bounded Promotion/Voucher projections (the honest method the
# User/Group/ProductType read slices established): the platform's
# authoritative discount-policy rows (V223 promotions/vouchers +
# voucher_redemptions accounting) own the facts; DECLARED fields are
# owned facts only:
#   Promotion: id (typed global ID over the native key); name (the
#   row's own non-null name); type (ORDER — every platform promotion
#   is an order-level policy by the entity's own contract; CATALOGUE
#   stays inert enum vocabulary); startDate/endDate (the policy
#   window — OPTIONAL on the platform, so the wire nullability
#   diverges from Saleor's non-null startDate: the registered
#   nullability divergence row, never a fabricated epoch); createdAt/
#   updatedAt (the audit instants every BaseEntity row owns).
#   Voucher: id; name (optional row fact); code (the row's normalized
#   non-null code); usageLimit (the row's global redemption limit,
#   null = unlimited); used (the redemption-row COUNT — the owner's
#   own accounting seam, never a stored counter); startDate/endDate
#   (same optional-window nullability divergence);
#   applyOncePerCustomer (the truthful flattening of the row's
#   per-user limit — true exactly when the limit is 1; the richer
#   N-per-customer fact stays with the owner's admin surface: the
#   registered flattening divergence row); discountValueType (the
#   owner's PERCENTAGE/FIXED vocabulary, verbatim);
#   currency (the policy row's own ISO-4217 denomination).
# UNDECLARED fields, each with its reason (a declared-but-fake field
# would be the violation, not the absence):
#   Promotion.rules: the platform's promotion is ONE flat order-level
#   policy row, not Saleor's rule-based model — the reward
#   value/type/min-spend facts have no owning rule closure here yet.
#   Promotion/Voucher money surfaces (the voucher's discountValue:
#   Float and minSpent: Money, the rule rewardValue upstream): the
#   frozen money contract forbids binary float for authoritative
#   amounts (minor-unit integers stay authoritative internally);
#   declared only when the exact-decimal rendering decision lands —
#   the registry's "Decimal / PositiveDecimal money" row.
#   Voucher.type (VoucherTypeEnum SHIPPING/ENTIRE_ORDER/
#   SPECIFIC_PRODUCT): no voucher-type discrimination exists — every
#   platform voucher is an order-level subtotal discount.
#   Voucher.applyOncePerOrder: upstream semantics = applied to a
#   single cheapest eligible PRODUCT; the platform's own once-per-
#   order law is the redemption idempotency unique index — a
#   different fact, undeclared to avoid a false equality.
#   Voucher.singleUse / codes: the multi-code feature-preview model
#   has no owner (the platform's voucher carries ONE code with usage
#   limits — the `code` field carries it).
#   Voucher.onlyForStaff / minCheckoutItemsQuantity / categories /
#   collections / products / variants / countries: no owning facts.
#   Voucher.channelListings + the channel ROOT arguments: no channel
#   model exists (the PENDING-ADR commercial-context row).
#   Promotion/Voucher.externalReference: no external-ID column exists
#   on either policy row.
#   The metadata family (metadata/privateMetadata/metafield(s)) on
#   both types: no owning metadata capability yet.
#   Both translations + Promotion.events/ description: JSON: no
#   translation owner, no promotion event log, no description fact.
# TEMPORAL RENDERING: Saleor's DateTime scalar renders as ISO-8601
# String (the house no-new-scalar decision the User.dateJoined /
# NeighborhoodPost.createdAt declarations established — the registered
# DateTime scalar divergence row).
# The declared-but-unexecuted root arguments (externalReference,
# channel, where/filter, the deprecated query, before/last) answer
# explicit classified IllegalArgumentExceptions at runtime — the
# staffUsers precedent — never a silent no-op, never fake success.
# The sort vocabularies are Saleor's own enums, declared verbatim:
# promotions executes NAME and CREATED_AT (the owning NON-NULL keyset
# columns; START_DATE/END_DATE are the optional window columns that
# cannot carry deterministic keyset cursors under the house map-based
# cursor contract and answer the explicit classified error); vouchers
# executes CODE alone (deprecated upstream but the only owned
# deterministic keyset field) — NAME/START_DATE/END_DATE (optional
# columns), VALUE/MINIMUM_SPENT_AMOUNT (channel-scoped money upstream
# + the frozen money contract), TYPE (no discrimination) and
# USAGE_LIMIT (optional column) answer the explicit classified error,
# as does the deprecated nested sortBy.channel.
# =====================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Query additions (append to the shared root type Query)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
type Query {
    # "Look up a voucher by ID or external reference." — the Saleor
    # voucher lookup (MANAGE_DISCOUNTS → ADMIN here, enforced in the
    # owning pricing use case). The id executes through the typed
    # global-ID codec: an unknown but well-formed ID answers null (the
    # safe absence); a malformed or mistyped global ID answers the
    # codec's classified validation error — never a raw UUID fallback.
    # externalReference (no external-ID column) and channel (no
    # channel model — the PENDING-ADR row) stay declared (the exact
    # Saleor argument shape) but answer an explicit classified error —
    # a recorded, tested boundary, not a silent no-op.
    voucher(
    """ID of the voucher."""
    id: ID

    """
    External ID of the voucher (no external-ID column on this platform — an explicit classified error).
    """
    externalReference: String

    """Slug of a channel for which the data should be returned (no channel model on this platform — an explicit classified error)."""
    channel: String
    ): Voucher

    # "List of the shop's vouchers." — the Saleor voucher list with its
    # countable-connection envelope (edges/pageInfo/totalCount,
    # byte-shape from the pinned schema). FORWARD-ONLY keyset paging on
    # this first slice: first/after ride the platform's ScrollPosition
    # keyset contract (the staffUsers/permissionGroups/productTypes
    # precedent — cursors identify a row's sort key (code, id), never
    # an absolute offset); before/last stay declared (the exact Saleor
    # argument shape) but answer an explicit classified error until a
    # backward scroll exists. filter, the deprecated query and channel
    # are likewise the declared wire shape with an explicit
    # not-yet-supported error. The sort vocabulary is Saleor's
    # VoucherSortField enum: CODE (deprecated upstream) executes as the
    # real keyset sort, deterministic with the id tiebreaker; every
    # other field answers the explicit not-implemented error.
    vouchers(
    """Filtering options for vouchers."""
    filter: VoucherFilterInput

    """Sort voucher."""
    sortBy: VoucherSortingInput

    """Search vouchers by name or code."""
    query: String @deprecated(reason: "Use `filter.search` input instead.")

    """Slug of a channel for which the data should be returned."""
    channel: String

    """Return the elements in the list that come before the specified cursor."""
    before: String

    """Return the elements in the list that come after the specified cursor."""
    after: String

    """Retrieve the first n elements from the list."""
    first: Int

    """Retrieve the last n elements from the list."""
    last: Int
    ): VoucherCountableConnection

    # "Look up a promotion by ID or external reference." — the Saleor
    # promotion lookup (MANAGE_DISCOUNTS → ADMIN here, enforced in the
    # owning pricing use case). The id executes through the typed
    # global-ID codec: an unknown but well-formed ID answers null (the
    # safe absence); a malformed or mistyped global ID answers the
    # codec's classified validation error — never a raw UUID fallback.
    # externalReference (no external-ID column) stays declared (the
    # exact Saleor argument shape) but answers an explicit classified
    # error — a recorded, tested boundary, not a silent no-op.
    promotion(
    """ID of the promotion."""
    id: ID

    """
    External ID of the promotion (no external-ID column on this platform — an explicit classified error).
    """
    externalReference: String
    ): Promotion

    # "List of the promotions." — the Saleor promotion list with its
    # countable-connection envelope (edges/pageInfo/totalCount,
    # byte-shape from the pinned schema). FORWARD-ONLY keyset paging on
    # this first slice: first/after ride the platform's ScrollPosition
    # keyset contract (the staffUsers/permissionGroups/productTypes
    # precedent — cursors identify a row's sort key (name|createdAt,
    # id), never an absolute offset); before/last stay declared (the
    # exact Saleor argument shape) but answer an explicit classified
    # error until a backward scroll exists. where is likewise the
    # declared wire shape with an explicit not-yet-supported error.
    # The sort vocabulary is Saleor's PromotionSortField enum: NAME and
    # CREATED_AT (the owning non-null keyset columns) execute as the
    # real keyset sorts, deterministic with the id tiebreaker;
    # START_DATE/END_DATE (the optional policy-window columns) answer
    # the explicit not-implemented error.
    promotions(
    """Where filtering options for promotions."""
    where: PromotionWhereInput

    """Sort promotions."""
    sortBy: PromotionSortingInput

    """Return the elements in the list that come before the specified cursor."""
    before: String

    """Return the elements in the list that come after the specified cursor."""
    after: String

    """Retrieve the first n elements from the list."""
    first: Int

    """Retrieve the last n elements from the list."""
    last: Int
    ): PromotionCountableConnection
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The bounded Promotion projection — see the block comment above for
# the closure policy. id is the typed global ID over the native
# promotions key; type is ORDER (every platform promotion is an
# order-level policy by the entity's own contract); the window and
# audit instants are ISO-8601 strings (the house no-new-scalar
# decision), with startDate OPTIONAL on the platform (the registered
# nullability divergence).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
type Promotion {
    """The ID of the promotion — typed global ID (opaque, never a raw UUID)."""
    id: ID!

    """Name of the promotion (the policy row's own name)."""
    name: String!

    """
    The type of the promotion — ORDER on this platform: every promotion row is an order-level policy (the entity's own contract).
    """
    type: PromotionTypeEnum

    """Start date of the promotion (ISO-8601; null when the policy row opens an unbounded window)."""
    startDate: String

    """End date of the promotion (ISO-8601; null when the policy row has no end)."""
    endDate: String

    """Date time of promotion creation (ISO-8601)."""
    createdAt: String!

    """Date time of last update of promotion (ISO-8601)."""
    updatedAt: String!
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The bounded Voucher projection — see the block comment above for
# the closure policy. id is the typed global ID over the native
# vouchers key; used is the redemption-row count (the owner's own
# accounting seam); applyOncePerCustomer is the truthful flattening of
# the per-user limit (true exactly when the limit is 1); the window
# instants are ISO-8601 strings, both OPTIONAL on the platform (the
# registered nullability divergence).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
type Voucher {
    """The ID of the voucher — typed global ID (opaque, never a raw UUID)."""
    id: ID!

    """The name of the voucher (null when the policy row carries none)."""
    name: String

    """The code of the voucher (the row's normalized uppercase code)."""
    code: String

    """
    The number of times a voucher can be used (the row's global redemption limit; null = unlimited).
    """
    usageLimit: Int

    """Usage count of the voucher (redemption rows counted — never a stored counter)."""
    used: Int!

    """The start date and time of voucher (ISO-8601; null when the policy row opens an unbounded window)."""
    startDate: String

    """The end date and time of voucher (ISO-8601; null when the policy row has no end)."""
    endDate: String

    """
    Determine if the voucher usage should be limited to one use per customer (the row's per-user limit == 1; a limit of N>1 or unlimited renders false).
    """
    applyOncePerCustomer: Boolean!

    """Determines a type of discount for voucher - value or percentage."""
    discountValueType: DiscountValueTypeEnum!

    """Currency code for voucher (the policy row's own ISO-4217 denomination)."""
    currency: String
}

# Saleor's connection envelope for countable promotion lists —
# declared (not runtime-generated) so the exact Saleor shape stands,
# including totalCount. Spring's ConnectionTypeDefinitionConfigurer
# skips already-declared connection types (the measured
# declared-types-skip behavior the UserCountableConnection/
# GroupCountableConnection/ProductTypeCountableConnection
# declarations recorded), so this declaration wins and the generated
# connections elsewhere are untouched. pageInfo reuses the EXISTING
# shared PageInfo type — not redeclared.
type PromotionCountableConnection {
    """Pagination data for this connection."""
    pageInfo: PageInfo!

    edges: [PromotionCountableEdge!]!

    """A total count of items in the collection."""
    totalCount: Int
}

type PromotionCountableEdge {
    """The item at the end of the edge."""
    node: Promotion!

    """A cursor for use in pagination (the row's keyset sort key)."""
    cursor: String!
}

# Saleor's connection envelope for countable voucher lists — same
# declared-not-generated rule as PromotionCountableConnection above;
# pageInfo reuses the EXISTING shared PageInfo type — not redeclared.
type VoucherCountableConnection {
    """Pagination data for this connection."""
    pageInfo: PageInfo!

    edges: [VoucherCountableEdge!]!

    """A total count of items in the collection."""
    totalCount: Int
}

type VoucherCountableEdge {
    """The item at the end of the edge."""
    node: Voucher!

    """A cursor for use in pagination (the row's keyset sort key)."""
    cursor: String!
}

# Saleor's promotion where-filter input — the declared wire shape of
# the where argument (see promotions: an explicit classified error
# until the owning query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: ids
# carries the scalar filter surface; name (its StringFilterInput
# closure), startDate/endDate (DateTimeFilterInput), isOldSale, type
# (PromotionTypeEnumFilterInput), metadata (its heavy MetadataFilter
# closure) and the AND/OR combinators stay undeclared until an owning
# capability exists — any where use answers the classified
# not-implemented error before field-level semantics matter, and a
# Dashboard query naming an undeclared sub-field fails schema
# validation loudly (never a silent no-op).
input PromotionWhereInput {
    ids: [ID!]
}

# Saleor's voucher filter input — the declared wire shape of the
# filter argument (see vouchers: an explicit classified error until
# the owning query capability exists). BOUNDED closure: search/ids
# carry the scalar filter surface; status (DiscountStatusEnum list),
# timesUsed (IntRangeInput), discountType (VoucherDiscountType list),
# started (DateTimeRangeInput) and metadata (its heavy MetadataFilter
# closure) stay undeclared until an owning capability exists — the
# same declared-shape rule the StaffUserInput/ProductTypeFilterInput
# precedents established.
input VoucherFilterInput {
    search: String
    ids: [ID!]
}

# Saleor's promotion sorting input and field vocabulary — the full
# pinned enum is declared verbatim; NAME and CREATED_AT execute as
# the real forward-only keyset sorts (the owning non-null columns,
# id tiebreaker); START_DATE/END_DATE (the optional policy-window
# columns) answer the explicit not-implemented error. direction
# reuses the EXISTING shared OrderDirection enum — not redeclared.
input PromotionSortingInput {
    """Specifies the direction in which to sort promotions."""
    direction: OrderDirection!

    """Sort promotions by the selected field."""
    field: PromotionSortField!
}

enum PromotionSortField {
    """Sort promotions by name."""
    NAME

    """Sort promotions by start date."""
    START_DATE

    """Sort promotions by end date."""
    END_DATE

    """Sort promotions by creation date."""
    CREATED_AT
}

# Saleor's promotion type vocabulary — declared verbatim; ORDER is the
# owning fact (every platform promotion is an order-level policy),
# CATALOGUE stays inert SDL vocabulary (never emitted by this
# platform).
enum PromotionTypeEnum {
    CATALOGUE
    ORDER
}

# Saleor's discount value type vocabulary — declared verbatim; the
# owner's PERCENTAGE/FIXED row vocabulary renders through it exactly.
enum DiscountValueTypeEnum {
    FIXED
    PERCENTAGE
}

# Saleor's voucher sorting input and field vocabulary — the full
# pinned enum is declared verbatim (CODE deprecated upstream with no
# reason string in the pinned schema); CODE executes as the real
# forward-only keyset sort (the row's non-null normalized code, id
# tiebreaker); NAME/START_DATE/END_DATE (optional columns),
# VALUE/MINIMUM_SPENT_AMOUNT (channel-scoped money upstream + the
# frozen money contract), TYPE (no voucher-type discrimination) and
# USAGE_LIMIT (optional column) answer the explicit not-implemented
# error, as does the deprecated nested channel. direction reuses the
# EXISTING shared OrderDirection enum — not redeclared.
input VoucherSortingInput {
    """Specifies the direction in which to sort vouchers."""
    direction: OrderDirection!

    """Specifies the channel in which to sort the data."""
    channel: String @deprecated(reason: "Use root-level channel argument instead.")

    """Sort vouchers by the selected field."""
    field: VoucherSortField!
}

enum VoucherSortField {
    """Sort vouchers by code."""
    CODE @deprecated

    """
    Sort vouchers by name.

    Added in Saleor 3.18.
    """
    NAME

    """Sort vouchers by start date."""
    START_DATE

    """Sort vouchers by end date."""
    END_DATE

    """
    Sort vouchers by value.

    This option requires a channel filter to work as the values can vary between channels.
    """
    VALUE

    """Sort vouchers by type."""
    TYPE

    """Sort vouchers by usage limit."""
    USAGE_LIMIT

    """
    Sort vouchers by minimum spent amount.

    This option requires a channel filter to work as the values can vary between channels.
    """
    MINIMUM_SPENT_AMOUNT
}
